# crossroads_02 — TWO WAYS IN
#
# BACKLOG A2.  ⚠ This is the SOURCE; `maps/crossroads_02.json` +
# `maps/crossroads_02_markers.json` beside it are BUILT from it by
# `scripts/build_maps.sh` and are what `make play MAP=crossroads_02` loads.
# `tests/a2_the_maps.loft` asserts the two still agree.
#
# ⚠ It is also playable directly, without building:
#     make play SCRIPT=maps/crossroads_02.keys
#
# ⚠⚠ A map holds the GROUND and the MARKERS and nothing else.  A `crew`
# or a `schedule` line here would be authored, played, and then silently
# dropped by the save — the run's wave list is the seven-wave default
# every `PlayState` starts with (`waves.loft::wave_list_default`).
#
# starter_01's neck, mirrored, with the core between them — and BOTH
# spawn markers feed the list once it is armed.  ⚠⚠ It is the one map
# here where PARKING IS THE WRONG ANSWER: holding the east lane reads
# t222 and sitting on the core t228, while shuttling between the two
# reads t250 (`@M045`).  `plans/17` § T3 measured exactly that about
# helpers — two shuttling clear all 205 robots where the same two
# parked reach 5 of 7 — and this is the ground it happens on.
#
# ⚠ It was NOT true of the first version of this map, and the reason is
# worth knowing: the spawns sat 16 hexes out, inside the forward tower's
# reach of 15, so both lanes were shelled as they arrived and every
# parking position landed within 7 ticks of every other.  Moving the
# spawns out past the guns is what gave the drive something to be worth.
echo crossroads_02: two ways in, and you can only stand in one of them

at 0 0 1

palette 5

# The home field, in the middle.
drag   -4  -5    4  -5
drag   -4  -4    4  -4
drag   -4  -3    4  -3
drag   -4  -2    4  -2
drag   -4  -1    4  -1
drag   -4   0    4   0
drag   -4   1    4   1
drag   -4   2    4   2
drag   -4   3    4   3
drag   -4   4    4   4
drag   -4   5    4   5

# The east neck and the field beyond it.
drag    5  -2    9  -2
drag    5  -1    9  -1
drag    5   0    9   0
drag    5   1    9   1
drag    5   2    9   2
drag   10  -6   24  -6
drag   10  -5   24  -5
drag   10  -4   24  -4
drag   10  -3   24  -3
drag   10  -2   24  -2
drag   10  -1   24  -1
drag   10   0   24   0
drag   10   1   24   1
drag   10   2   24   2
drag   10   3   24   3
drag   10   4   24   4
drag   10   5   24   5
drag   10   6   24   6

# The west neck and the field beyond it.
drag   -9  -2   -5  -2
drag   -9  -1   -5  -1
drag   -9   0   -5   0
drag   -9   1   -5   1
drag   -9   2   -5   2
drag  -24  -6  -10  -6
drag  -24  -5  -10  -5
drag  -24  -4  -10  -4
drag  -24  -3  -10  -3
drag  -24  -2  -10  -2
drag  -24  -1  -10  -1
drag  -24   0  -10   0
drag  -24   1  -10   1
drag  -24   2  -10   2
drag  -24   3  -10   3
drag  -24   4  -10   4
drag  -24   5  -10   5
drag  -24   6  -10   6

# ── A wall across each neck, each with its lane left open. ──
palette 9
click    7  -2
click    7  -1
click    7   1
click    7   2
click   -7  -2
click   -7  -1
click   -7   1
click   -7   2

# ── The markers ──
do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click    0   0
marker   0   0 target

# Two towers per lane — the same pair starter_01 has, twice.
do cycle_kind
click    3   0
click    5   0
click   -3   0
click   -5   0
marker   3   0 tower
marker  -5   0 tower

# The east spawn, facing home — 22 out, past the forward tower's 15.
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click   22   0
marker  22   0 spawn 3

# The west spawn, facing home.  Three more rotations bring the
# place-direction back round to 0, which is EAST.
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click  -22   0
marker -22   0 spawn 0

do toggle_mode

count markers 7 7
kind 0 0 grass
kind 7 1 wall
kind -7 1 wall
kind 7 0 grass
